From: Mahdi Taziki <61482609+Mhd-tz@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winemac: Set the cursor again when the pointer returns to a macOS full-screen window.

In macOS full screen the pointer can leave the window's content without leaving the app: at the top edge macOS
reveals the menu bar and title bar, and on displays with a camera housing the strip beside it is outside the window.
AppKit shows its own arrow there, but Wine's cursor cache (cursorIsCurrent) still says the client's cursor is set, so
back in the window the arrow stays until the game changes its cursor (owner, Warcraft III, 2026-11-01: "the cursor
stays like that for a while"). Now, for a window in macOS full screen (NSWindowStyleMaskFullScreen) and an active app,
when the pointer comes back from a screen edge or from outside the content, the client's cursor is set again once (a
hidden cursor is hidden again, as patch 0005 does for Wine's own full-screen windows). Ordinary movement inside the
window changes nothing, so there's no flicker.

Provenance (recorded by AnvilMac, 2026-11-01):
  Written for AnvilMac by Claude Code; not submitted upstream.
  Base: wine-11.19, commit 455e3509b98a, with patches 0002, 0005, 0006 and 0015 of this series.
  File: dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m (Wine, LGPL-2.1-or-later).
  License of this change: LGPL-2.1-or-later. Copyright 2026 Mahdi Taziki.
  Checked: builds (local winemac.so); behaviour pending the owner's game session.

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
@@ -70,6 +70,10 @@
 
 /* The pointer reached a screen edge while a fullscreen window had the cursor hidden. */
 static BOOL pointerVisitedScreenEdge;
+
+/* The pointer left a macOS full-screen window's content (screen edge, revealed menu or title bar, the strip beside the
+   camera housing), where AppKit shows its own arrow without Wine knowing. */
+static BOOL pointerLeftNativeFullscreenContent;
 
 static BOOL point_at_screen_edge(NSPoint point)
 {
@@ -1395,6 +1399,7 @@
     - (void) handleMouseMove:(NSEvent*)anEvent
     {
         WineWindow* targetWindow;
+        WineWindow* previousTargetWindow = lastTargetWindow;
         BOOL drag = [anEvent type] != NSEventTypeMouseMoved;
 
         if ([windowsBeingDragged count])
@@ -1551,6 +1556,27 @@
         }
         else
             pointerVisitedScreenEdge = FALSE;
+
+        /* macOS full screen: once the pointer is back from an edge or from outside the content, set the client's
+           cursor (or its hide) again, once. Our cache can't tell that AppKit replaced it meanwhile. */
+        if (lastTargetWindow && ([lastTargetWindow styleMask] & NSWindowStyleMaskFullScreen) && [NSApp isActive])
+        {
+            if (point_at_screen_edge([NSEvent mouseLocation]))
+                pointerLeftNativeFullscreenContent = TRUE;
+            else if (pointerLeftNativeFullscreenContent)
+            {
+                pointerLeftNativeFullscreenContent = FALSE;
+                cursorIsCurrent = FALSE;
+                if (clientWantsCursorHidden && cursorHidden)
+                {
+                    [NSCursor unhide];
+                    cursorHidden = FALSE;
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        else if (!lastTargetWindow && previousTargetWindow &&
+                 ([previousTargetWindow styleMask] & NSWindowStyleMaskFullScreen))
+            pointerLeftNativeFullscreenContent = TRUE;
 
         [self updateCursor:FALSE];
     }
